    {
      "_id": "mmSwallow0000000",
      "_key": "!actors.items!mmGiantFrog00000.mmSwallow0000000",
      "name": "Swallow (Swallowed)",
      "type": "action",
      "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-rows-needles-purple.webp",
      "system": {
        "active": true,
        "description": "<p>The giant frog swallows a Small or smaller target it is grappling. While swallowed, the target isn't Grappled but has the Blinded and Restrained conditions, and it has Total against attacks and other effects outside the frog.</p><p>While swallowing the target, the giant frog can't use Bite, and if the giant frog dies, the swallowed target is no longer Restrained and can escape from the corpse using 5 feet of movement, exiting with the Prone condition.</p><p>At the end of the giant frog's next turn, the swallowed target takes 5 (2d4) Acid damage. If that damage doesn't kill it, the giant frog disgorges it, causing it to exit Prone.</p>",
        "definition": {
          "schemaVersion": 1,
          "id": "action:srd-swallow-swallowed",
          "costs": {
